    "knowledge_point": "Determining Whether Two Events are Mutually Exclusive",
    "problem": "Given $P(A)=\\frac{1}{4},$ $P(B)=\\frac{3}{10},$ and $P(A\\cup B)=\\frac{19}{40},$ determine whether $A$ and $B$ are mutually exclusive events.",
    "worked_solution": "To check if $A$ and $B$ are mutually exclusive, we must check that $P(A\\cap B)=0.$\n\nWe can calculate $P(A\\cap B)$ using the addition law:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(A\\cup B) & =P(A)+P(B)-P(A\\cap B) \\\\ \\frac{19}{40} & =\\frac{1}{4}+\\frac{3}{10}-P(A\\cap B) \\\\ P(A\\cap B) & =\\frac{1}{4}+\\frac{3}{10}-\\frac{19}{40} \\\\  & =\\frac{10+12-19}{40} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{40} \\\\  & \\ne 0\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $A$ and $B$ are not mutually exclusive events.",
