    "reasoning": "All 16 mathematical answers agree with their own captured Math Academy worked solutions. For q-87289, inclusion–exclusion gives P(A∩B)=1/4+3/10−19/40=3/40≠0, so the events are not mutually exclusive. For q-87305 and q-87308, subtracting P(B) from P(A∪B) gives 8/15 and 2/25. For q-12554, the remaining deck contains 3 aces and 12 spades with no overlap, giving 15/51=5/17. For q-120545, 10 novels and 3 illustrated science books among 19 remaining books give 13/19. For q-49570, a_n=x²(x/3)^n converges exactly when 0<x≤3; equality gives a constant sequence. For q-141322, the positive geometric ratio x²/4 must be at most 1, giving 0<x≤2. For q-11827, y=a(x−3)²−5 and (0,4) imply a=1. For q-115434, y=ax² and (−5,2) imply a=2/25, equivalently x²=(25/2)y. For q-160013, comparing real and imaginary coefficients gives a=3/4 and b=√3. For q-8408, multiplying by 2i gives p+iq=4−6i. For q-160049, dividing by 3+i gives p+qi=3/2−i/2. The graph endpoints for q-73349 give the secant slope (7−2)/(4−(−5))=5/9; those for q-125248 give (−4−(−3))/(3−(−5))=−1/8. For q-2305, the secant slope is 4 and f′(c)=6c+1, giving c=1/2. For q-2342, the secant slope is 3 and f′(c)=2c−2, giving c=5/2. Both c values lie inside their required intervals. Confirmation is based on captured worked solutions, not an inferred grading key.",
